    "title": "pandas.api.types.is_period_dtype — pandas 3.1.0.dev0 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.api.types.is_period_dtype#\n\n- \npandas.api.types.is_period_dtype(*arr_or_dtype* )[source]#\n- Check whether an array-like or dtype is of the Period dtype. Deprecated since version 2.2.0: Use isinstance(dtype, pd.PeriodDtype) instead. \n  - Parameters:\n    - **arr_or_dtype** array-like or dtype\n    - The array-like or dtype to check.\n  - Returns:\n    - boolean\n    - Whether or not the array-like or dtype is of the Period dtype.\n See also \n  - `api.types.is_timedelta64_ns_dtype`\n  - Check whether the provided array or dtype is of the timedelta64[ns] dtype.\n  - `api.types.is_timedelta64_dtype`\n  - Check whether an array-like or dtype is of the timedelta64 dtype.\n Examples >>> from pandas.api.types import is_period_dtype >>> is_period_dtype(object) False >>> is_period_dtype(pd.PeriodDtype(freq=\"D\")) True >>> is_period_dtype([1, 2, 3]) False >>> is_period_dtype(pd.Period(\"2017-01-01\")) False >>> is_period_dtype(pd.PeriodIndex([], freq=\"Y\")) True",
    "markdown_length": 960,
